From c69d0c1128e87a240730e4c5a9bbffeb034fef17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrews Danyo <andrews@local>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 21:42:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Add Pre-Orders: phone-in orders with deposit/balance
 tracking

For clients who call to place an order and come later for pickup or
delivery once they finish paying. Built as an extension of the
existing sales_orders table (not a separate feature) so Fulfill,
stock deduction, and P&L reporting all work automatically with zero
duplication:

- New columns: customer_phone, is_preorder, fulfillment_method
  (pickup/delivery), delivery_address, deposit_amount, amount_paid.
  Included in schema.sql for fresh installs, plus a standalone
  db/migration_preorders.sql (ALTER TABLE, additive only) for
  existing databases -- running schema.sql again would wipe data.
- POST /sales-orders now accepts and stores these fields; a deposit
  collected at creation counts as the first payment.
- New POST /sales-orders/{id}/payment endpoint to record additional
  payments as a client pays down their balance over time.
- New PreOrderForm (client name/phone, pickup vs delivery, delivery
  address when applicable, line items, optional deposit, live
  balance-due preview) and PreOrdersTable (client contact, payment
  status, Record Payment and Fulfill actions -- reusing the exact
  same location-aware stock check already proven in the main Sales
  Orders Fulfill flow) at /admin/pre-orders, linked from the sidebar.

Verified end-to-end: create with deposit -> pay remaining balance ->
fulfill -> stock correctly deducted and status flips to shipped.
